      "model_answer": "Latest Malaysian labour-market snapshot (DOSM, Aug 2026):\n\nUnemployment edged down to 2.9% in Aug 2026 from 3.0% in Jul, with participation at 71.0% and 16.87m employed. This is a two-month national trend, not a sector or role-level signal. [1]\n\nThe July baseline (3.0% unemployment, 70.9% participation, 16.85m employed) shows the small month-on-month improvement, but only two months are available, so the direction is preliminary. [2]\n\nNational aggregate only; no sector, occupation or vacancy detail, and only two months are shown.\n\nPractical advice (not a measured market finding): Pair these headline rates with sector/occupation data before drawing hiring or skills conclusions.\n\nSource method: web search ran, but no usable discovered page was fetched. These links are predefined detail/reference pages fetched live or from the labelled recent cache.",
