      "model_answer": "Software engineering demand in Malaysia is tied to modernisation and scalable app needs.\n\nThe 2026 Malaysian guide says software engineering opportunities span full-stack, backend and frontend development, with demand linked to legacy-system modernisation and scalable consumer applications. It names financial services, telecommunications, software services, semiconductor and electronics as hiring sectors. [1]\n\nThe same guide says organisations are hiring software engineers to build scalable, low-latency applications, modernise technology systems and deliver software projects while meeting strict security requirements. [2]\n\nThis is a 2026 Malaysian recruitment-firm guide, not a national vacancy census or measured role growth rate.\n\nPractical advice (not a measured market finding): Focus on full-stack, backend/frontend, security and scalable-systems skills.\n\nSource method: web search ran, but no usable discovered page was fetched. These links are predefined detail/reference pages fetched live or from the labelled recent cache.",
