      "model_answer": "Relevant skills depend on the role; the passages point to core engineering and front-end foundations.\n\nThe US occupational reference frames software work around testing/validation, programming, documentation, and analyzing user needs and requirements for feasibility within time and cost constraints. [1]\n\nFor front-end web development, the MDN curriculum highlights semantic HTML, CSS, and JavaScript fundamentals, while noting version control and testing can start with basics and grow over a career. [2]\n\nUS occupational reference and a global front-end curriculum; neither measures Malaysian demand or current hiring popularity.\n\nPractical advice (not a measured market finding): Practice building small projects that combine requirements analysis, coding, testing, and version control.\n\nSource method: web search found additional pages. This explanation cites predefined detail/reference pages fetched separately, not search snippets.",
